# fixedbugs, defect 092, lane b13-unit, 2026-10-06: a count C reads through
# a pointer, `getsockopt`'s `optlen`, is an `@` cell, and panel 194's R7
# compares the value it holds on the way in with the record lent whole. 4096
# bytes for a record of four: the program aborts before C runs, naming the
# record's parameter, the count and the unit, and `a`, printed first, shows
# nothing was written. Before that sitting `counted_by` refused an `@`
# sibling, so this binding had no checked spelling at all, and without the
# mark it wrote 4092 bytes over the stack at `check` 0.
extern "fixedbugs-092-records.h"
    record One tag one
        a: i32
    function fill_len(@buf: One counted_by n, @n: u32) -> i64

function main()
    o: One @ One(a: 0)
    n: u32 @ 4096
    print(o.a)
    print(fill_len(@o, @n))
    print(o.a)
